    "url": "https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/56225774/180022425-f11defbb-6a08-4d91-be28-6bd585b06677.png",
    "local_path": "/app/.harbor_assets/bug_screenshot_1.png",
    "description": "Effarig's Reality description panel showing the text 'Glyph levels are temporarily capped to 2000, rarity is unaffected.' The value 2000 is circled in blue, highlighting that it is rendered as a raw bare integer rather than being passed through the game's active notation formatter (formatInt). In-game, all numbers should respect the player's chosen notation; this one bypasses it because the template string uses bare ${Effarig.glyphLevelCap} interpolation instead of ${formatInt(Effarig.glyphLevelCap)}."
  },
  {
    "role": "bug_screenshot",
    "url": "https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/56225774/180022438-b4b56ef3-265d-4b48-869f-c6b969cb4650.png",
    "local_path": "/app/.harbor_assets/bug_screenshot_2.png",
    "description": "Pelle unlock-requirements panel showing 'You must have 17 rows of achievements to unlock Doomed.' and '16 / 17' below it. Both the static literal 17 and the dynamic completedRows value 16 are rendered as plain integers rather than notation-formatted values. The fix must replace the hardcoded '17' literal and the bare {{ completedRows }} binding with {{ formatInt(17) }} and {{ formatInt(completedRows) }} / {{ formatInt(17) }} so that all numbers in this panel respect the active notation."
  }
]

